import AxQM.Concrete.DeutschWireUniversality
import AxQM.Concrete.ReachableCircuits

/-!
# The Deutsch gate is universal: reachable circuits dense in `U(2ⁿ)` up to phase (N&C Ex 4.44)

*(N&C Exercise 4.44 — the universality density core.)*

This file specialises the **generic** reachable-circuit density
(`Concrete/ReachableCircuits.lean`) to the Deutsch gate `G = C²(iR_x(πα))`: the matrix gates `G`
reaches on the wires of an `m`-qubit register generate a submonoid of circuits whose closure fills
`U(2ⁿ)` up to an (unobservable) global phase — the **universality density core** of Exercise 4.44,
for `α` irrational.

## What is generic and what is Deutsch-specific

The whole §4.5/§4.3 register assembly — every unitary is a product of `Toffoli`/`CNOT`/`NOT` and
uncontrolled single-qubit wire gates, each approximated up to a global phase, the phases combining —
is the shared skeleton `exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_reachableCircuitsOf`
(`Concrete/ReachableCircuits.lean`), parameterised over an abstract single-qubit gate set `S`. The
**only** Deutsch-specific input is which single-qubit set and its per-wire density:

* `S = deutschWireGateSubmonoid α` (`Concrete/DeutschWireUniversality.lean`) — the submonoid `G`
  reaches on a wire, generated by its dense `x`-axis orbit `⟨iR_x(πα)⟩` and the phase gate `S`
  (with `S†`); its per-wire closure fills `U(2)` up to a global phase precisely when `α` is
  irrational (`exists_phase_smul_singleQubitOnWire_mem_closure_deutschWireGateSubmonoid`).

Exercise 4.43's `Concrete/FourGateUniversality.lean` is the sibling specialisation, at
`S = reachableRotations θ` (`cos θ = 3/5`).

## The construction and results

* `deutschReachableGateSet enc α` / `deutschReachableCircuits enc α` — the generic
  `reachableGateSetOf` / `reachableCircuitsOf` at `S = deutschWireGateSubmonoid α`: the
  `≤ 2`-control reversible gates `IsToffoliPermGate` together with, on every wire `j`, the
  single-qubit gates
  `singleQubitOnWire enc j g` with `g ∈ deutschWireGateSubmonoid α`, and the submonoid they
  generate.
* `exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_deutschReachableCircuits` — **the density core**: for `α`
  irrational, an encoding `enc : (Fin m → Fin 2) ≃ Fin d` with `m ≥ 1`, and *any* `U ∈ U(d)`, some
  global phase `e^{ia}` makes `e^{ia} • U` a limit of `deutschReachableCircuits enc α` — the
  reachable circuits are dense in `U(d)` up to a global phase. A one-line instantiation of the
  generic density at the Deutsch per-wire density `α` irrational.

## Scope: this is the abstract density core, not yet the faithful terminal

The single-qubit gates `G` reaches on a wire (`deutschWireGateSubmonoid α`) are realised from `G`
only **with control ancillas** — the dense `x`-axis needs two control wires held at `|1⟩`
(`C²(R_x(β))` acts as `R_x(β)` on the target only on the `|11⟩` control subspace), the phase gate
`S` a control-wire placement. This file states density over the *abstract* gate set
`deutschReachableGateSet` (as Exercise 4.43's `FourGateUniversality` states it over its abstract
`reachableGateSet`). Realising these gates from `G` on register wires with ancillas goes through
the ancilla compression `⟨11|_anc ⊗ I⟩ · (G-placement) · |11⟩_anc ⊗ I⟩ = data gate`.
-/

namespace AxQM.Concrete

open Matrix

variable {m d : ℕ}

/-- **The reachable gate set of the Deutsch gate** — the generic `reachableGateSetOf` at the Deutsch
single-qubit submonoid `S = deutschWireGateSubmonoid α`: the `≤ 2`-control reversible gates
`IsToffoliPermGate enc G` together with, on every wire `j`, the single-qubit gates
`singleQubitOnWire enc j g` with `g ∈ deutschWireGateSubmonoid α` (the gates `G = C²(iR_x(πα))`
reaches on a wire). -/
noncomputable def deutschReachableGateSet (enc : (Fin m → Fin 2) ≃ Fin d) (α : ℝ) :
    Set (Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℂ) :=
  reachableGateSetOf enc (deutschWireGateSubmonoid α : Set (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ))

/-- **The reachable circuits of the Deutsch gate** — the submonoid generated by
`deutschReachableGateSet enc α` (the generic `reachableCircuitsOf` at
`S = deutschWireGateSubmonoid α`), i.e. the matrix incarnation of the circuits assembled from `G`.
Universality is the statement that its closure fills `U(d)` up to a global phase
(`exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_deutschReachableCircuits`). -/
noncomputable def deutschReachableCircuits (enc : (Fin m → Fin 2) ≃ Fin d) (α : ℝ) :
    Submonoid (Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℂ) :=
  reachableCircuitsOf enc (deutschWireGateSubmonoid α : Set (Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ))

/-- **Universality of the Deutsch gate `G = C²(iR_x(πα))`, density core** (N&C Exercise 4.44). For
`α` irrational, an encoding `enc : (Fin m → Fin 2) ≃ Fin d` of an `m`-qubit register with at least
one qubit, and *any* unitary `U ∈ U(d)`, some global phase `e^{ia}` makes `e^{ia} • U` a limit of
reachable circuits: `e^{ia} • U ∈ closure ↑(deutschReachableCircuits enc α)`.

In the finite-dimensional product topology on `Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℂ`, closure is approximation
to arbitrary accuracy, so this is exactly: **the circuits built from the gates `G` reaches on
register wires are dense in `U(d)` up to an (unobservable) global phase** — the universality core of
Exercise 4.44. A one-line instantiation of the generic
`exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_reachableCircuitsOf` (`Concrete/ReachableCircuits.lean`) at the
Deutsch per-wire density `exists_phase_smul_singleQubitOnWire_mem_closure_deutschWireGateSubmonoid`
(`α` irrational) — the sole Deutsch-specific input.

This states density over the *abstract* gate set `deutschReachableGateSet`; its single-qubit
members are realised from `G` on register wires with control ancillas as described in the module
docstring. -/
theorem exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_deutschReachableCircuits [Nontrivial (Fin m → Fin 2)]
    {α : ℝ} (hα : Irrational α) (enc : (Fin m → Fin 2) ≃ Fin d)
    {U : Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℂ} (hU : U ∈ Matrix.unitaryGroup (Fin d) ℂ) :
    ∃ a : ℝ, Complex.exp ((a : ℂ) * Complex.I) • U
      ∈ closure (↑(deutschReachableCircuits enc α) : Set (Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℂ)) :=
  exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_reachableCircuitsOf enc
    (exists_phase_smul_singleQubitOnWire_mem_closure_deutschWireGateSubmonoid hα enc) hU

end AxQM.Concrete
